IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 66 and 66.1 -- OVERPAYMENTS, RECOVERY, REMEDIES FOR OFFICIAL ERROR, AND
-- CANCELLING A BENEFIT.
--
-- Section 66 puts a person who was paid a benefit they were not entitled to (or too much of it) under a duty to
-- return it at once (subsection (1)), makes the amount a debt to the Crown (subsection (2)), and gives the
-- Minister the means of collecting it: set-off against other amounts payable (subsection (2.1)), a certificate
-- registered as a court judgment (subsections (2.2) to (2.6)), and garnishment of those who owe the debtor money
-- (subsections (2.7) and (2.8)). Subsection (3) lets the Minister remit the debt; subsections (4) and (5) oblige
-- the Minister to put right the effects of official error; subsection (6) takes the debt out of section 155.1
-- of the Financial Administration Act. Section 66.1 lets a beneficiary cancel a benefit and repay it, so that it is
-- treated as never payable.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: the facts that decide whether a person is entitled to a benefit (the whole of
-- Part II, piece cp3); interest payable under this Part and a penalty under section 90.1 (piece cp5); the Criminal
-- Code (not among the texts). Regulations 42 (hardship limit on set-off) and 46.2 (the 12 months for a
-- request to cancel and for repayment) are brought in with their figures, cited by the locator form
-- `src:C.R.C.-c.-385:N`; both lie in piece cr2's range of the Regulations.

§ `Section 66 -- return and recovery of benefit payment`

§§ `Section 66(1) and (2) -- return of the benefit payment, and the debt`

-- src:2194 | Return of benefit where recipient not entitled
-- src:2195 | 66 (1) A person or estate that has received or obtained by cheque or otherwise a benefit payment to which the person or estate is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which the person or estate is entitled, shall forthwith return the cheque or the amount of the benefit payment, or the excess amount, as the case may be.
@ref Act s 66(1) (src:2195)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit payment the person or estate has received or obtained` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person or estate is entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(1) — the amount the person or estate must at once return` `the amount of the benefit payment the person or estate has received or obtained` `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person or estate is entitled` MEANS
    -- "a benefit payment to which the person or estate is not entitled" (entitled to nothing) "or a benefit payment in
    -- excess of the amount ... to which the person or estate is entitled": the excess, nothing if there is none.
    max 0 (`the amount of the benefit payment the person or estate has received or obtained` MINUS `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person or estate is entitled`)

-- src:2196 | Recovery of amount of payment
-- src:2197 | (2) If a person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled, the amount of the benefit payment or the excess amount, as the case may be, constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref Act s 66(2) (src:2197)
GIVEN `the amount of the benefit payment the person has received or obtained` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2) — the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` `the amount of the benefit payment the person has received or obtained` `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled` MEANS
    -- The amount, or the excess amount, is a debt "recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of
    -- competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act".
    `s 66(1) — the amount the person or estate must at once return` `the amount of the benefit payment the person has received or obtained` `the amount of the benefit payment to which the person is entitled` GREATER THAN 0

-- src:2198 | Recovery of amount of interest
-- src:2199 | (2.01) Interest payable under this Part constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref Act s 66(2.01) (src:2199)
GIVEN `the amount is interest payable under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.01) — the interest is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` `the amount is interest payable under this Part` MEANS
    `the amount is interest payable under this Part`

-- src:2200 | Recovery of amount of penalty
-- src:2201 | (2.02) The amount of a penalty imposed on a person under section 90.1 constitutes a debt due to Her Majesty and is recoverable at any time in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by this Act.
@ref Act s 66(2.02) (src:2201)
GIVEN `the amount is a penalty imposed on the person under section 90.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.02) — the penalty is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` `the amount is a penalty imposed on the person under section 90.1` MEANS
    `the amount is a penalty imposed on the person under section 90.1`

§§ `Section 66(2.1) to (2.9) -- collecting the debt`

-- src:2202 | Set-off
-- src:2203 | (2.1) Where any amount is or becomes payable to the person or the person’s estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister, that indebtedness may, in the prescribed manner, be deducted and retained out of the amount payable.
@ref Act s 66(2.1) (src:2203)
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:442 | 42 For the purpose of subsection 66(2.1) of the Act, an amount of indebtedness that is owing may be deducted and retained out of the whole or any portion of a benefit that is payable to the person or the person’s estate or succession, under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister, that will recover the overpayment in a single payment or in instalments, in any amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person or the person’s estate or succession.
@ref Reg 42 (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:442)
GIVEN `the amount of the indebtedness` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister` IS A NUMBER
      `the largest amount that can be deducted without causing undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(2.1) — the most that may be deducted and retained out of an amount payable` `the amount of the indebtedness` `the amount payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister` `the largest amount that can be deducted without causing undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession` MEANS
    -- The indebtedness "may be deducted and retained out of the amount payable"; regulation 42 (piece cr2) allows a
    -- single payment or instalments, "in any amount that does not cause undue hardship". What is undue hardship is a
    -- judgment, taken as the third input.
    min `the amount of the indebtedness` (min `the amount payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister` `the largest amount that can be deducted without causing undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession`)

-- src:2204 | Certificates
-- src:2205 | (2.2) All or part of the amount of that indebtedness that has not been recovered may be certified by the Minister
-- src:2206 | (a) without delay, if in the Minister’s opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment; and
-- src:2207 | (b) in any other case, on the expiration of 30 days after the default.
@ref Act s 66(2.2) (src:2205-2207)
GIVEN `in the Minister's opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the Minister forms that opinion` IS A DATE
      `the day of the default` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 66(2.2) — the first day on which the Minister may certify the indebtedness that has not been recovered` `in the Minister's opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment` `the day the Minister forms that opinion` `the day of the default` MEANS
    -- (a): "without delay" once the Minister is of that opinion. (b): "on the expiration of 30 days after the default":
    -- the 30 days run from the day after the default, so the first day after they expire is the 31st day (NOTES.md,
    -- fork register).
    IF `in the Minister's opinion the person liable to pay the amount is attempting to avoid payment`
    THEN `the day the Minister forms that opinion`
    ELSE `the day of the default` PLUS 31

-- src:2208 | Judgment
-- src:2209 | (2.3) On production to the Federal Court, the certificate shall be registered in the Court. When it is registered, it has the same force and effect, and all proceedings may be taken, as if the certificate were a judgment obtained in the Court for a debt of the amount specified in the certificate.
@ref Act s 66(2.3) (src:2209)
GIVEN `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.3) — the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt` `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered` MEANS
    `the certificate has been produced to the Federal Court and registered`

-- src:2210 | Judgment
-- src:2211 | (2.4) A certificate registered under subsection (2.3) may also be registered in the superior court of a province as if it were a document evidencing a judgment of that court.
@ref Act s 66(2.4) (src:2211)
GIVEN `a certificate has been registered under subsection (2.3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.4) — the certificate may also be registered in the superior court of a province` `a certificate has been registered under subsection (2.3)` MEANS
    `a certificate has been registered under subsection (2.3)`

-- src:2212 | Costs
-- src:2213 | (2.5) All reasonable costs and charges for the registration of the certificate are recoverable in the same way as if they had been certified and the certificate registered under this section.
@ref Act s 66(2.5) (src:2213)
GIVEN `the costs and charges are reasonable and are for the registration of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.5) — the costs and charges are recoverable as if certified and the certificate registered` `the costs and charges are reasonable and are for the registration of the certificate` MEANS
    `the costs and charges are reasonable and are for the registration of the certificate`

-- src:2214 | Charge on land
-- src:2215 | (2.6) A document issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province evidencing a certificate in respect of a debtor registered under subsection (2.3) or (2.4) may be recorded for the purpose of creating security, or a charge, lien or legal hypothec, on land in a province, or on an interest in land in a province, held or owned by the debtor, in the same manner as a document evidencing a judgment of the superior court of the province against a person for a debt owing by the person may be recorded in accordance with the law of the province to create security, or a charge, lien or legal hypothec, on land, or an interest in land, held or owned by the person.
@ref Act s 66(2.6) (src:2215)
GIVEN `a certificate in respect of a debtor has been registered under subsection (2.3) or (2.4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a document evidencing the certificate has been issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the land or the interest in land in a province is held or owned by the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.6) — the document may be recorded to create security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on the debtor's land` `a certificate in respect of a debtor has been registered under subsection (2.3) or (2.4)` `a document evidencing the certificate has been issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province` `the land or the interest in land in a province is held or owned by the debtor` MEANS
    -- "in the same manner as a document evidencing a judgment of the superior court of the province ... may be
    -- recorded in accordance with the law of the province": the manner is the province's.
        `a certificate in respect of a debtor has been registered under subsection (2.3) or (2.4)`
    AND `a document evidencing the certificate has been issued by the Federal Court or by a superior court of a province`
    AND `the land or the interest in land in a province is held or owned by the debtor`

-- src:2216 | Garnishment
-- src:2217 | (2.7) If the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Part, the Minister may, by a notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person in whole or in part to the Receiver General on account of the second person’s liability.
@ref Act s 66(2.7) (src:2217)
GIVEN `the Minister knows or suspects that the person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has served a notice personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.7) — the person is required to pay the money otherwise payable to the debtor to the Receiver General` `the Minister knows or suspects that the person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Part` `the Minister has served a notice personally or by confirmed delivery service` MEANS
    -- "the money otherwise payable to the second person in whole or in part ... on account of the second person's liability".
        `the Minister knows or suspects that the person is or is about to become indebted or liable to make a payment to a person liable to make a payment to Her Majesty under this Part`
    AND `the Minister has served a notice personally or by confirmed delivery service`

-- src:2218 | Debt due to the Crown
-- src:2219 | (2.8) An amount not paid as required by a notice under subsection (2.7) is a debt due to Her Majesty.
@ref Act s 66(2.8) (src:2219)
GIVEN `a notice under subsection (2.7) required an amount to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount was not paid as the notice required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.8) — the amount not paid as required by the notice is a debt due to Her Majesty` `a notice under subsection (2.7) required an amount to be paid` `the amount was not paid as the notice required` MEANS
    `a notice under subsection (2.7) required an amount to be paid` AND `the amount was not paid as the notice required`

-- src:2220 | Proof of personal service
-- src:2221 | (2.9) If provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand, an affidavit of the person effecting service stating that
-- src:2222 | (a) the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case,
-- src:2223 | (b) such a request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed, and
-- src:2224 | (c) the person identifies as an exhibit attached to the affidavit a true copy of the request, notice or demand,
-- src:2225 | is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand.
@ref Act s 66(2.9) (src:2221-2225)
GIVEN `provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit of the person effecting service states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit identifies as an exhibit attached to it a true copy of the request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(2.9) — the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand` `the affidavit of the person effecting service states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` `the affidavit states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` `the affidavit identifies as an exhibit attached to it a true copy of the request, notice or demand` MEANS
        `provision is made by this Act or the regulations for personal service of a request for information or a notice or demand`
    AND `the affidavit of the person effecting service states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case`
    AND `the affidavit states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed`
    AND `the affidavit identifies as an exhibit attached to it a true copy of the request, notice or demand`

§§ `Section 66(3) to (6) -- remission, remedies for official error, the Financial Administration Act`

-- src:2226 | Remission of amount owing
-- src:2227 | (3) Notwithstanding paragraph 61(2)(b) and subsections (1) and (2) of this section, where a person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which he is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount of the benefit payment to which he is entitled, and the Minister is satisfied that
-- src:2228 | (a) the amount or excess of the benefit payment cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future,
-- src:2229 | (b) the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess of the benefit payment are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected,
-- src:2230 | (c) repayment of the amount or excess of the benefit payment would cause undue hardship to the debtor, or
-- src:2231 | (d) the amount or excess of the benefit payment is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error on the part of the Minister or an official of the Department of Employment and Social Development acting in an official capacity in the administration of this Act,
-- src:2232 | the Minister may, unless that person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment, remit all or any portion of the amount or excess of the benefit payment.
@ref Act s 66(3) (src:2227-2232)
GIVEN `the person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount to which the person is entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that repayment of the amount or excess would cause undue hardship to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error on the part of the Minister or an official of the Department of Employment and Social Development acting in an official capacity in the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` `the person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount to which the person is entitled` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future` `the Minister is satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected` `the Minister is satisfied that repayment of the amount or excess would cause undue hardship to the debtor` `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error on the part of the Minister or an official of the Department of Employment and Social Development acting in an official capacity in the administration of this Act` `the person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment` MEANS
    -- The four paragraphs are alternatives ("(a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ... or (d) ..."); the Minister's satisfaction is
    -- the input, and the power is withheld from a person convicted in connection with obtaining the payment.
        `the person has received or obtained a benefit payment to which the person is not entitled, or a benefit payment in excess of the amount to which the person is entitled`
    AND (   `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess cannot be collected within the reasonably foreseeable future`
         OR `the Minister is satisfied that the administrative costs of collecting the amount or excess are likely to equal or exceed the amount to be collected`
         OR `the Minister is satisfied that repayment of the amount or excess would cause undue hardship to the debtor`
         OR `the Minister is satisfied that the amount or excess is the result of erroneous advice or administrative error on the part of the Minister or an official of the Department of Employment and Social Development acting in an official capacity in the administration of this Act`)
    AND (NOT `the person has been convicted of an offence under any provision of this Act or of the Criminal Code in connection with the obtaining of the benefit payment`)

-- src:2233 | Where person denied benefit due to departmental error, etc.
-- src:2234 | (4) Where the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, any person has been denied
-- src:2235 | (a) a benefit, or portion thereof, to which that person would have been entitled under this Act,
-- src:2236 | (b) a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1, or
-- src:2237 | (c) an assignment of a retirement pension under section 65.1,
-- src:2238 | the Minister shall take such remedial action as the Minister considers appropriate to place the person in the position that the person would be in under this Act had the erroneous advice not been given or the administrative error not been made.
@ref Act s 66(4) (src:2234-2238)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, the person has been denied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit, or portion thereof, to which the person would have been entitled under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an assignment of a retirement pension under section 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(4) — the Minister must take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in` `the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, the person has been denied` `a benefit, or portion thereof, to which the person would have been entitled under this Act` `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1` `an assignment of a retirement pension under section 65.1` MEANS
    -- What action is appropriate is "as the Minister considers appropriate": the Minister's choice, not derived.
        `the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, the person has been denied`
    AND (   `a benefit, or portion thereof, to which the person would have been entitled under this Act`
         OR `a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1`
         OR `an assignment of a retirement pension under section 65.1`)

-- src:2239 | When person denied division
-- src:2240 | (5) Where the Minister is satisfied that a person has been denied a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 as a result of the provisions of a written agreement entered into or a court order made before June 4, 1986, the Minister shall take such remedial action as the Minister considers appropriate to place the person in the position that the person would be in under this Act had the division been approved, including attributing to that person the earnings that would have been attributed had the division been approved, if
-- src:2241 | (a) the agreement or order does not indicate that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under this Act; and
-- src:2242 | (b) all other criteria specified by or under this Act respecting divisions are met.
@ref Act s 66(5) (src:2240-2242)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been denied a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 as a result of the provisions of a written agreement entered into or a court order made before June 4, 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement or order does not indicate that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all other criteria specified by or under this Act respecting divisions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(5) — the Minister must take remedial action, including attributing the earnings that would have been attributed` `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been denied a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 as a result of the provisions of a written agreement entered into or a court order made before June 4, 1986` `the agreement or order does not indicate that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under this Act` `all other criteria specified by or under this Act respecting divisions are met` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been denied a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or 55.1 as a result of the provisions of a written agreement entered into or a court order made before June 4, 1986`
    AND `the agreement or order does not indicate that there be no division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under this Act`
    AND `all other criteria specified by or under this Act respecting divisions are met`

-- src:2243 | Exclusion of Financial Administration Act
-- src:2244 | (6) Section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act does not apply in relation to amounts owing to Her Majesty under this Part.
@ref Act s 66(6) (src:2244)
GIVEN `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(6) — section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies in relation to the amount` `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under this Part` MEANS
    -- NOTHING for an amount not owing under this Part: the subsection says nothing about it.
    IF `the amount is owing to Her Majesty under this Part`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 66.1 -- request to cancel benefit`

-- src:2247 | Exception
-- src:2248 | (1.1) Subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of a retirement pension in favour of a disability benefit where an applicant for a disability benefit under this Act or under a provincial pension plan is in receipt of a retirement pension and the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of entitlement to the disability benefit in or after the month for which the retirement pension first became payable.
@ref Act s 66.1(1.1) (src:2248)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `an applicant for a disability benefit under this Act or under a provincial pension plan is in receipt of a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of entitlement to the disability benefit` IS A DATE
      `the month for which the retirement pension first became payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66.1(1.1) — subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of the retirement pension` kind `an applicant for a disability benefit under this Act or under a provincial pension plan is in receipt of a retirement pension` `the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of entitlement to the disability benefit` `the month for which the retirement pension first became payable` MEANS
    -- "the cancellation of a retirement pension in favour of a disability benefit ... deemed to have become disabled ...
    -- in or after the month for which the retirement pension first became payable". (Where the person became disabled
    -- earlier, regulation 46.2(2) to (2.2), piece cr2, has its own routes.)
        (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a retirement pension` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `an applicant for a disability benefit under this Act or under a provincial pension plan is in receipt of a retirement pension`
    AND `the month of a date` `the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of entitlement to the disability benefit` AT LEAST `the month of a date` `the month for which the retirement pension first became payable`

-- src:2245 | Request to cancel benefit
-- src:2246 | 66.1 (1) A beneficiary may, in prescribed manner and within the prescribed time interval after payment of a benefit has commenced, request cancellation of that benefit.
@ref Act s 66.1(1) (src:2246)
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:475 | 46.2 (1) A beneficiary may submit to the Minister, within the interval between the date of commencement of payment of the benefit and the expiration of 12 months after that date, a request in writing that the benefit be cancelled.
@ref Reg 46.2(1) (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:475)
GIVEN `the day payment of the benefit commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the request is made` IS A DATE
      `the request is made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) is taken out by subsection (1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` `the day payment of the benefit commenced` `the day the request is made` `the request is made in the prescribed manner` `subsection (1) is taken out by subsection (1.1)` MEANS
    -- "in prescribed manner and within the prescribed time interval after payment of a benefit has commenced": by
    -- regulation 46.2(1) (piece cr2) in writing, from the commencement of payment to the expiry of 12 months after it.
    -- The Minister then "shall grant" a request submitted in accordance with it (reg 46.2(3)).
        `the request is made in the prescribed manner`
    AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date` `the day the request is made` `the day payment of the benefit commenced` (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 12)
    AND (NOT `subsection (1) is taken out by subsection (1.1)`)

-- src:2249 | Effect of cancellation
-- src:2250 | (2) Where a request made under subsection (1) or under a substantially similar provision of a provincial pension plan is granted and the amount of the benefits paid is repaid within the prescribed time or, in the case of a provincial pension plan, the time provided thereunder, that benefit shall be deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period in question.
@ref Act s 66.1(2) (src:2250)
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:480 | (4) If a request referred to in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act is granted under this section, the amount described in that subsection shall be repayable within the time beginning on the granting of the request and ending on the expiration of 12 months following the month in which the request is granted.
@ref Reg 46.2(4) (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:480)
GIVEN `a request made under subsection (1) or under a substantially similar provision of a provincial pension plan is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the request is granted` IS A DATE
      `the day the amount of the benefits paid is repaid` IS A DATE
      `the amount is repaid within the time provided under the provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` `a request made under subsection (1) or under a substantially similar provision of a provincial pension plan is granted` `the request is under a provincial pension plan` `the day the request is granted` `the day the amount of the benefits paid is repaid` `the amount is repaid within the time provided under the provincial pension plan` MEANS
    -- "repaid within the prescribed time or, in the case of a provincial pension plan, the time provided thereunder":
    -- by regulation 46.2(4) (piece cr2) from the granting of the request to the expiry of 12 months following the
    -- month in which it is granted, that is, before the first day of the 13th month after the month of granting.
        `a request made under subsection (1) or under a substantially similar provision of a provincial pension plan is granted`
    AND (IF `the request is under a provincial pension plan`
         THEN `the amount is repaid within the time provided under the provincial pension plan`
         ELSE (   `the day the amount of the benefits paid is repaid` AT LEAST `the day the request is granted`
              AND `the day the amount of the benefits paid is repaid` LESS THAN (`add months` (`the month of a date` `the day the request is granted`) 13)))
